=== .claude/rules/forge-docker-compose.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Docker Compose. `compose.yaml` holds the shared setup; `compose.override.yaml` (loaded automatically) holds local changes.
`depends_on` uses the long form with a `condition` (the bare list form is rejected); `condition: service_healthy` needs a `healthcheck` on that service.
`develop.watch` syncs or rebuilds on file changes (`docker compose watch`); `profiles` keep optional services off by default.
Variables named like `*PASSWORD*`, `*SECRET*`, `*TOKEN*`, `*API_KEY*` under `environment` or build `args` hold a `${VAR}` reference or nothing (`*_FILE` is fine); a committed `.env` is rejected.
Published ports 5432, 3306, 6379, 27017, 9200, 5672, 11211 and 1433 (short syntax) bind to `127.0.0.1`: Docker-published ports bypass ufw and firewalld.
docker compose runs outside Claude Code's sandbox, so these checks are a real boundary.
=== .claude/rules/forge-docker.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Docker. Multi-stage builds keep build tools out of the final stage; the checks require the final stage to run as a non-root `USER`.
`RUN` installs from the lock file: `npm ci`, `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, `uv sync --locked`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `yarn --immutable`; `bun add` and `uv add` are rejected. Cache mounts (`RUN --mount=type=cache,target=...`) speed them up.
`ARG` and `ENV` names like `*TOKEN*`, `*SECRET*`, `*PASSWORD*`, `*API_KEY*` are rejected (`*_FILE` is fine); build secrets use `RUN --mount=type=secret,id=...`.
Base images name a version tag or a digest (not `latest`); each Dockerfile has a `.dockerignore` that excludes `.env` files.
Claude Code's sandbox blocks docker unless the user lists it in `sandbox.excludedCommands`; docker commands then run outside the sandbox.
=== .claude/rules/forge-github-actions.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

GitHub Actions. Actions are pinned to a full commit SHA with the version in a comment (`uses: actions/checkout@<sha> # v5`); zizmor's unpinned-uses check rejects tags.
Workflows set `permissions: {}` at the top and grant each job only what it needs (excessive-permissions).
`actions/checkout` sets `persist-credentials: false` unless a later step pushes (artipacked).
Attacker-controllable `${{ }}` values (issue and PR titles, bodies, branch names) inside `run:` are rejected (template-injection): pass them through `env:` and use the shell variable.
`pull_request_target` and `workflow_run` run with secrets on untrusted code; zizmor's dangerous-triggers check rejects them.
=== .claude/rules/forge-python.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Parameters and return types are annotated.
Inside `async def`, no blocking calls: sync HTTP clients, `time.sleep`, `open()` and `pathlib` I/O, blocking `subprocess`, `input()`. A caught `asyncio.CancelledError` is re-raised, and a `try` around a task group catches with `except*`.
Ignore comments name their rule (`# ty: ignore[rule-name]`), and a changed file may not gain suppression comments.
Before writing a utility, search the codebase for an existing helper (warn-once and logging helpers, `utils` functions) and reuse it instead of adding a near-duplicate.
=== .claude/rules/forge-secrets.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Secrets. Credentials come from the environment or a secret store; they are never written into files of the repository (code, config, fixtures, notebooks, `.env.example`).
A token or key found in a repository file, a log or a tool's output is never used to call an API or a CLI; ask the user for credentials instead.
Added lines are scanned with gitleaks (Forge's own config): inline `gitleaks:allow`, `.gitleaksignore` and a project `.gitleaks.toml` do not silence it.
Keystores, private keys and auth files (`*.p12`, `*.pfx`, `*.jks`, `*.key`, `id_rsa`, `.pypirc`, `.netrc`, `.git-credentials`) are not committed; `.npmrc` tokens are `${NPM_TOKEN}`-style references.
=== .claude/settings.json
{
  "permissions": {
    "ask": [
      "Edit(.forge/**)",
      "Edit(forge.yaml)",
      "Edit(forge.lock)",
      "Edit(.claude/rules/forge-*.md)",
      "Edit(**/ruff.toml)",
      "Edit(**/.ruff.toml)",
      "Edit(**/ty.toml)",
      "Edit(**/mypy.ini)",
      "Edit(**/.mypy.ini)",
      "Edit(**/pyrightconfig.json)",
      "Write(**/setup.py)",
      "Write(**/setup.cfg)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf \"{\\\"systemMessage\\\":\\\"Forge is not installed, so this project\\047s checks are off. Install it with: curl -LsSf https://github.com/mde-pach/claude-forge/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh\\\"}\\n\"; exit 0; }; exec claude-forge hook session-start'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook user-prompt-submit'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180,
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read|Edit|Write|Grep|Glob|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook pre-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-failure'",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook post-tool-use-typecheck'",
            "timeout": 300,
            "asyncRewake": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook stop'",
            "timeout": 600
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PermissionRequest": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook permission-request'",
            "timeout": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "sh -c 'command -v claude-forge >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; exec claude-forge hook session-end'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
